Title: Simple Web Stack (one server, LAMP-like with Nginx)
URL: www.foobar.com (DNS: foobar.com with a "www" A record -> 8.8.8.8)

ASCII diagram:
[User] -> Internet -> [Server 8.8.8.8] -> [Nginx -> App Server -> Code] -> [MySQL]

Request path:
1) User -> https://www.foobar.com
2) DNS resolves www.foobar.com -> 8.8.8.8 (A record)
3) Browser opens TCP (HTTP/HTTPS) to 8.8.8.8
4) Nginx serves static / proxies dynamic to App Server
5) App executes code, queries MySQL, returns response

Explain:
- Server: machine providing services over a network
- Domain name: human-friendly name resolved by DNS to an IP
- DNS record for 'www': A (IPv4) or AAAA (IPv6)
- Web server (Nginx): HTTP(S) termination, static files, reverse proxy
- Application server: runs business logic, handles requests, talks to DB
- Database (MySQL): persistent storage (SQL/ACID)
- Protocol: HTTP/HTTPS over TCP/IP (TLS for HTTPS)

Issues:
- SPOF: single server (failure = outage)
- Maintenance downtime: restarts interrupt service
- No scale: limited by one box; no horizontal scaling
